2. Inside the `shared/components` folder, create a new component, e.g., `my-shared-component.component.ts`.
3. Define the component in the file `my-shared-component.component.ts`:
```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-my-shared-component',
  template: '<p>Shared component {{ title }}</p>'
})
export class MySharedComponent {
  title = 'My Shared Component';
}
```
In this example, we've created a simple component that displays the text "My Shared Component".

4. Add the component to your Angular module(s) that need to use it. You can do this by importing the component in the module's ` declarations` array and adding it to the `entryComponents` array (if you're using a lazy-loaded module).

For example, let's say you want to use the `MySharedComponent` in multiple modules. You can add it to a shared module, e.g., `shared.module.ts`:
```typescript
import { NgModule } from '@angular/core';
import { CommonModule } from '@angular/common';
import { MySharedComponent } from './components/my-shared-component.component';

@NgModule({
  imports: [CommonModule],
  declarations: [MySharedComponent],
  exports: [MySharedComponent]
})
export class SharedModule { }
```
In this example, we've created a `SharedModule` that imports the `CommonModule` and exports the `MySharedComponent`.

